Z||000000||KnightRyder31||01-17-2001||09:24 AM||||This morning around 7:25AM I went to start my car for school. When I turned the key it just made clicking sounds. So I waited a couple of seconds and tryed again, this time it turned over, but only for a sec. I kept trying and all of the times that I tryed it either made a clicking noise, or it turned over but didn't start.<BR>Then I waited about 10mins, and tryed again, this time it started up. So I'm a little confused. I'm afraid to take it anywhere, because it may not start again.<P>HELP!!!||||reg||8
Z||000001||deceler8||01-17-2001||09:30 AM||||Has it snowed recently ?<P>If so, check to see if your battery is covered with snow. This will cause a slow drain which will kill the battery.<P>I covered my battery and connections with a piece of carpet to keep the snow from filling that area...haven't had the problem since.||||reg||1
Z||000002||KnightRyder31||01-17-2001||10:48 AM||||Well, it just started...so I am kind of puzzled. What the hell was its problem this mourning?!?!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||KnightRyder31||01-17-2001||10:52 AM||||I also have had some crappy idle problems...could this be related?<BR>My car almost stalls out in Reverse, and it has slower acceleration then usual. While at a stop light, it idles down to like 500, and then shoots back up to around 1100, and back down again constantly. It already has stalled out in reverse before. Could it be bad gas from the station?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||KnightRyder31||01-17-2001||10:54 AM||||And it also likes to idle high while either parked or at a light, like up to 1300RPM...so its hard to keep the car at a stop. So it either idles very low, or to high.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||01-17-2001||12:21 PM||||Check the battery terminals and starter connections for corrosion (or they are loose). Cleaning them should help. It sounds like the corroded portion isn't making good contact and trying to start it "heats" the corrosion up and then you get better contact. Either that or the battery is starting to go bad.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||KnightRyder31||01-17-2001||07:56 PM||||Thanks guys.<BR>But do you have any sugestions about the ideling problems?||||reg||1
Z||000007||MrPBody||01-17-2001||08:55 PM||||I'll second Oreif's advice.  Clean all the battery and starter connections, including ground cable connection to the engine, and maybe check tightness of starter bolts.<P>Idle problem?  I dunno.  What kind of engine do you have?  Anyhow, check electrical connections first.  That might even help the idle.  Check alternator output, too.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by MrPBody (edited 01-17-2001).]||||reg||1
